"Columbia Tools","C12MPX6","Columbia 12"" Stainless Steel Mud Pan",92.95,"<p>Introducing the Columbia Mud Pan—the first in our new line of premium hand tools, designed for professionals who demand durability, comfort, and performance. Crafted from heavy-gauge stainless steel, this mud pan is built to withstand the toughest tasks, while its watertight, laser-welded seams ensure long-lasting reliability. With tapered ends and sides for a secure grip, this tool is ready to handle any job with ease. Plus, every Columbia Mud Pan comes with a free soft, non-slip rubber grip for enhanced comfort and ease of use.</p> <p>Now available in three convenient sizes—12″, 14″, and 16″—there’s a Columbia Mud Pan perfect for any project. The mud pans are sold in packs of 6 to dealers, but you have the flexibility to sell them individually to your customers.</p> <p><strong>Lifetime Warranty:</strong></p> <p>We stand by the quality and craftsmanship of our products. Each Columbia Mud Pan is backed by a lifetime warranty, ensuring you can rely on it for years of hard work.</p> <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Heavy-Gauge Stainless Steel: Engineered for strength and longevity, this mud pan resists wear and tear for reliable, long-term use.</li> <li>Watertight Laser-Welded Seams: Prevents leaks, even under heavy-duty conditions, for consistent performance.</li> <li>Comfortable Grip: Tapered ends and sides provide a secure, ergonomic hold for better control and comfort.</li> <li>Straight Edges: Ideal for wiping joint knives clean, ensuring a mess-free and efficient work process.</li> <li>Complimentary Rubber Grip: Every Columbia Mud Pan comes with a FREE soft, non-slip rubber grip for enhanced comfort and ease of use—adding even more value to this already premium tool.</li> <li>Available in 12″, 14″, and 16″ Sizes: Choose the right size for your specific needs and project requirements.</li> </ul>"
"Columbia Tools","C14MPX6","Columbia 14"" Stainless Steel Mud Pan",95.93,"<p>Introducing the Columbia Mud Pan—the first in our new line of premium hand tools, designed for professionals who demand durability, comfort, and performance. Crafted from heavy-gauge stainless steel, this mud pan is built to withstand the toughest tasks, while its watertight, laser-welded seams ensure long-lasting reliability. With tapered ends and sides for a secure grip, this tool is ready to handle any job with ease. Plus, every Columbia Mud Pan comes with a free soft, non-slip rubber grip for enhanced comfort and ease of use.</p> <p>Now available in three convenient sizes—12″, 14″, and 16″—there’s a Columbia Mud Pan perfect for any project. The mud pans are sold in packs of 6 to dealers, but you have the flexibility to sell them individually to your customers.</p> <p><strong>Lifetime Warranty:</strong></p> <p>We stand by the quality and craftsmanship of our products. Each Columbia Mud Pan is backed by a lifetime warranty, ensuring you can rely on it for years of hard work.</p> <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Heavy-Gauge Stainless Steel: Engineered for strength and longevity, this mud pan resists wear and tear for reliable, long-term use.</li> <li>Watertight Laser-Welded Seams: Prevents leaks, even under heavy-duty conditions, for consistent performance.</li> <li>Comfortable Grip: Tapered ends and sides provide a secure, ergonomic hold for better control and comfort.</li> <li>Straight Edges: Ideal for wiping joint knives clean, ensuring a mess-free and efficient work process.</li> <li>Complimentary Rubber Grip: Every Columbia Mud Pan comes with a FREE soft, non-slip rubber grip for enhanced comfort and ease of use—adding even more value to this already premium tool.</li> <li>Available in 12″, 14″, and 16″ Sizes: Choose the right size for your specific needs and project requirements.</li> </ul>"
"Columbia Tools","C1H","Columbia 4' Extendable One Handle",27.9,"<p>The Columbia One Handle is designed to work with your Columbia products universally. From the Nail Spotters and Angleheads, to the Rollers and the Corner Boxes, the One system allows you to lighten your load and still utilize all the finishing tools you love. Add a Tomalock adaptor and you can even use this handle with Flat Boxes if necessary. &nbsp;This One handle is all you’ll need.</p> <p>Features:</p> <ul> <li>Comes in two fixed lengths (4′ and 18″) and a 3 – 5′ extendible version</li> <li>AHA Adaptor needed to use with Angleheads</li> <li>Handmade from U.S. billet aluminum and steel components</li> <li>Machined in our state of the art facility in Canada</li> <li>Hard anodized tube</li> <li>Comfort grips</li> <li>Thickest, strongest and lightest handle on the market</li> </ul>"
"Columbia Tools","C1HEXT","Columbia 3'-5' Extendable One Handle",92.1,"<p>The Columbia One Handle is designed to work with your Columbia products universally. From the Nail Spotters and Angleheads, to the Rollers and the Corner Boxes, the One system allows you to lighten your load and still utilize all the finishing tools you love. Add a Tomalock adaptor and you can even use this handle with Flat Boxes if necessary. &nbsp;This One handle is all you’ll need.</p> <p>Features:</p> <ul> <li>Comes in two fixed lengths (4′ and 18″) and a 3 – 5′ extendible version</li> <li>AHA Adaptor needed to use with Angleheads</li> <li>Handmade from U.S. billet aluminum and steel components</li> <li>Machined in our state of the art facility in Canada</li> <li>Hard anodized tube</li> <li>Comfort grips</li> <li>Thickest, strongest and lightest handle on the market</li> </ul>"
"Columbia Tools","CBNCR","Columbia Outside Bullnose Corner Roller",55.12,"<p>Offering four different profiles, Columbia Outside Corner Rollers will be sure to make your tape on bead setting job faster.</p> <p>Features:</p> <ul> <li>Available in Standard, Bullnose, Wide and Micro (European)</li> <li>Hand made from U.S. aluminum and steel components</li> <li>Machined in our state of the art facility in Canada</li> </ul>"
"Columbia Tools","CC","Columbia Corner Cobra Adjustable Roller",245.62,"<p>The Corner Cobra is an amazing time saving tool. It allows the user to roll out No-Coat and other structural corner beads at almost all inside and outside angles. We have heard back from users that it does it quicker and better, which is to us a home run. Another one of our patented products that is changing the time it takes to finish a job.</p> <p>Features:</p> <ul> <li>Works on inside and outside angles from 85 to 180 degrees</li> <li>Sets No-Coat 350 and 425 as well as regular tapes</li> <li>Tracks the centre and outside edge leaving only a knife feather</li> <li>Fits Corner Roller handles</li> <li>Shocks allow for imperfect angles and settings</li> <li>Hand made from U.S. billet aluminum and steel components</li> <li>Machined in our state of the art facility in Canada</li> </ul>"
"Columbia Tools","CEXT90","Columbia External 90 Mud Applicator",78.82,"<p>The Columbia External 90 ° Mud Applicator works for all sizes of outside bead as it puts out 3 layers of mud, one in the middle, and one on each side. The amount of pressure applied to the tube will dictate how much mud you need for larger or smaller bead. These applicators are machined from solid billet aluminum and are very accurate as their Delrin wheels glide along the wall.</p> <p>Features:</p> <ul> <li>Hand made from U.S. aluminum and steel components</li> <li>Machined in our state of the art facility in Canada</li> </ul>"
